From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 06:05:08 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] iommu: apple-dart: leave a DART no device uses alone
 after a deep sleep

After a firmware-driven resume, every DART that runtime PM had
suspended gets its saved state written back in the noirq phase, and
the write-back starts by reading the stream registers. That includes a
DART whose consumers are all disabled, as the J604's SIO DART is (SIO
and the AES engine are both off in its tree). It has no power-domains
of its own, so genpd powers nothing for it, and its block may well be
off after the wake: the read then aborts, as the radio's DART did
before its host learnt to restore it.

A DART with no stream in any group has nothing to restore. Skip it,
unless apple_dart.restore_unused is set. Its runtime resume restores
it as before, should a consumer ever bind.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
---
 drivers/iommu/apple-dart.c | 27 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 27 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/iommu/apple-dart.c b/drivers/iommu/apple-dart.c
index 3176df5265..1203ba49a7 100644
--- a/drivers/iommu/apple-dart.c
+++ b/drivers/iommu/apple-dart.c
@@ -6561,6 +6561,27 @@ module_param(wake_restore_suspended, bool, 0644);
 MODULE_PARM_DESC(wake_restore_suspended,
 		 "After a real sleep, restore runtime-suspended DARTs in noirq (default) or at their runtime resume");
 
+/*
+ * A DART no device uses (its consumers' nodes disabled, as the J604's SIO DART) has nothing to
+ * restore after a real sleep, and nothing may have powered its block: a DART without
+ * power-domains of its own gets none from genpd. Off, the restore's first read aborts, as the
+ * radio's DART did. Its runtime resume restores it should a consumer ever bind.
+ */
+static bool restore_unused;
+module_param(restore_unused, bool, 0644);
+MODULE_PARM_DESC(restore_unused,
+		 "After a deep sleep, also restore the DARTs no device uses (default off)");
+
+static bool apple_dart_in_use(struct apple_dart *dart)
+{
+	unsigned int sid;
+
+	for (sid = 0; sid < dart->num_streams; sid++)
+		if (dart->sid2group[sid])
+			return true;
+	return false;
+}
+
 static __maybe_unused int apple_dart_resume_noirq(struct device *dev)
 {
 	struct apple_dart *dart = dev_get_drvdata(dev);
@@ -6582,6 +6603,12 @@ static __maybe_unused int apple_dart_resume_noirq(struct device *dev)
 
 	ret = pm_runtime_force_resume(dev);
 
+	if (!ret && pm_resume_via_firmware() && pm_runtime_status_suspended(dev) &&
+	    !READ_ONCE(restore_unused) && !apple_dart_in_use(dart)) {
+		dev_dbg(dev, "no device uses it: not restored after sleep\n");
+		return 0;
+	}
+
 	/*
 	 * A real sleep took the registers even of a DART runtime PM had suspended, which
 	 * force_resume leaves alone. Its consumer's firmware may DMA through it before
-- 
